 submenu for Visit us\nOpen days and visits\nAttractions\nFor schools and colleges\nLocation\nAlumni\nLibrary and Collections\nBusiness School\nThings To Do\nAbout us\nHow to contact us\nSearch durham.ac.uk\nSearch\nClose search\nHome\nStudy\nInternational\nApplication Guidance\nInternational\nExplore\nInternational\nStudying in the UK\nsubmenu for \"Studying in the UK\"\nWhy Durham?\nEuropean (Erasmus+) Exchange\nNon-European Exchange\nFee-Paying Study Abroad\nAgents and Representatives\nInternational Campus Visits\nRegional Information\nsubmenu for \"Regional Information\"\nAfrica & Middle East\nCentral & South Asia\nMainland China\nEast Asia and Australasia\nEurope\nLatin America & Caribbean\nNorth America\nSouth East Asia\nUK\nApplication Guidance\nsubmenu for \"Application Guidance\"\nInternational Country-Specific Qualifications\nEnglish Language Requirements\nSupport Services\nHow To Apply\nUK Qualifications\nFees and Funding\nsubmenu for \"Fees and Funding\"\nFee Status and Payment\nForeign Loans\nInternational Scholarships, Awards and Bursaries\nLiving Costs\nApplication Fees and Post Offer Deposits (PG)\nCollege Residence Charges\nVisas\nsubmenu for \"Visas\"\nConfirmation of Acceptance for Studies (CAS)\nApplying for a Student Visa\nStudent Visa Requirements\nYour Family\nStudent Visa: Money Required\nStudying as a Visitor\nArrivals\nsubmenu for \"Arrivals\"\nInternational Meet and Greet service\nInformation for pre-sessional students\nWhat to bring\nLife in Durham and the UK\nThings to do in Durham\nMeet and Greet FAQs\nPathway Programmes\nsubmenu for \"Pathway Programmes\"\nInternational Foundation Year\nPre-Masters\nEnglish Preparation\nOpen menu\nStudying in the UK\nShow submenu for Studying in the UK\nWhy Durham?\nEuropean (Erasmus+) Exchange\nNon-European Exchange\nFee-Paying Study Abroad\nAgents and Representatives\nInternational Campus Visits\nRegional Information\nShow submenu for Regional Information\nAfrica & Middle East\nCentral & South Asia\nMainland China\nEast Asia and Australasia\nEurope\nLatin America & Caribbean\nNorth America\nSouth East Asia\nUK\nApplication Guidance\nShow submenu for Application Guidance\nInternational Country-Specific Qualifications\nEnglish Language Requirements\nSupport Services\nHow To Apply\nUK Qualifications\nFees and Funding\nShow submenu for Fees and Funding\nFee Status and Payment\nForeign Loans\nInternational Scholarships, Awards and Bursaries\nLiving Costs\nApplication Fees and Post Offer Deposits (PG)\nCollege Residence Charges\nVisas\nShow submenu for Visas\nConfirmation of Acceptance for Studies (CAS)\nApplying for a Student Visa\nStudent Visa Requirements\nYour Family\nStudent Visa: Money Required\nStudying as a Visitor\nArrivals\nShow submenu for Arrivals\nInternational Meet and Greet service\nInformation for pre-sessional students\nWhat to bring\nLife in Durham and the UK\nThings to do in Durham\nMeet and Greet FAQs\nPathway Programmes\nShow submenu for Pathway Programmes\nInternational Foundation Year\nPre-Masters\nEnglish Preparation\nApplication Guidance\nThe Universities and Colleges Admissions Service (UCAS) handles applications for all undergraduate courses eg BA, BSc, MEng, MPhys, MSci. Durham University handles all postgraduate degree applications directly.\nUndergraduates may apply for up to five courses and you should list your choices in alphabetical order, not in order of preference.\u202fYou will need to include the UCAS code for each university you apply to \u2013 for Durham University choose D86 \u2013 and the code for the course or courses you are interested in.\u202f Postgraduate students use our Applicant Portal.\nRead More\nHow to Apply\nAs an international undergraduate applicant, as well as submitting your application through UCAS you will also need to send scanned copies of your qualifications (including your score in any English language test you have undertaken) to our Recruitment and Admissions Office.\u202fPlease make sure that you include your UCAS personal identification number (PID), your name, and your date of birth in your email.\nUCAS and Postgraduate Information\nUndergraduate Study\nFor detailed information on the undergraduate application process, please visit our undergraduate section.\nUCAS Apply Now\nApply for your chosen course. The UCAS site is packed with tools, including a handy personal statement builder. For Durham University choose D86.\nPostgraduate Study (Taught)\nFor detailed information on the postgraduate taught application process, please visit our postgraduate taught courses section.\nPostgraduate Study (Research)\nFor detailed information on the postgraduate research application process, please visit our postgraduate research degrees section.\nFees and Post Offer Deposits\nFind out more information on application fees and post-offer deposits for international students (postgraduate only).\nPostgraduate Applicant Portal\nFor most postgraduate degrees, you must apply through Durham\u2019s Applicant Portal. You don\u2019t have to submit your application all in one go.\nDedicated Support Services\nDurham University has dedicated support services to assist our international applicants from application right through to graduation to ensure that you gain the most from your studies and your time in the UK.\nThe International Office offers advice and support for anyone thinking of applying to Durham University from outside of the UK and staff travel regularly to attend international education fairs and meet prospective students.\nYou can contact the International Office and our support services at any time with any questions you may have:\nGeneral Enquires: Please visit: Ask Us\nRegional contacts: Please visit: Regional Pages\nInternational Campus Visit: International Campus Visits\nImmigration Enquiries: Please visit: Immigration Durham\nGlobal Opportunities Enquires: Please visit: Global Durham\nContact Durham University\nAbout us\nDurham University on Bluesky\nDurham University on Twitter\nDurham University on Facebook\nDurham University on LinkedIn\nDurham University on YouTube\nDurham University on Instagram\nDurham University on TikTok\nThe University\nAbout us\nJobs\nContact us\nVisit us\nOur Colleges\nAcademic Departments\nCeremonies\nStatements and policies\nNotices\nStatement on Modern Slavery\nFreedom of expression\nWebsite accessibility\nStudent complaints and non-academic misconduct\nSafeguarding\nBusiness services\nHelping business\nAnalytical services\nGlobal Durham\nInternational Consortia\nResearch and partnerships\nUseful links\nLearn Ultra\nBanner Self-Service\nStaff directory\nTechnician Commitment\nDU Hub (Internal)\nIT help and support\nThe Palatine Centre\nDurham University\nStockton Road\nDurham\nDH1 3LE\nCharitable status\nDisclaimer\nTrading name\nCookie notice\nPrivacy notices\n\u00a92026 Durham University", "links": [["Skip to main content", "https://www.durham.ac.uk/study/international/application-guidance/#main-content"], ["", "https://www.durham.ac.uk/"], ["", "https://www.durham.ac.uk/"], ["Alumni", "https://www.durham.ac.uk/alumni/"], ["Library and Collections", "https://www.durham.ac.uk/departments/library/"], ["Business School", "https://www.durham.ac.uk/business/"], ["Things To Do", "https://www.durham.ac.uk/things-to-do/"], ["About us", "https://www.durham.ac.uk/about-us/"], ["How to contact us", "https://www.durham.ac.uk/about-us/how-to-contact-us/"], ["Study", "https://www.durham.ac.uk/study/"], ["Undergraduate", "https://www.durham.ac.uk/study/undergraduate/"], ["Postgraduate", "https://www.durham.ac.uk/study/postgraduate/"], ["International", "https://www.durham.ac.uk/study/international/"], ["Employability", "https://www.durham.ac.uk/study/employability/"], ["Wider Student Experience", "https://www.durham.ac.uk/colleges-and-student-experience/"], ["Our Colleges", "https://www.durham.ac.uk/colleges-and-student-experience/colleges/"], ["Enrichment activities", "https://www.durham.ac.uk/colleges-and-st